From: AdrielOrihuela <adriel.orihuela.m@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 01:15:21 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Save what commands change through the server.properties mode

Every vanilla setting the running server changes, /whitelist on,
setMaxPlayers, the view distance and the rest of the nineteen mutable
ones, goes through Settings.MutableValue#update. That is now where the
change is saved, through ServerProperties.set: into server.properties
with the mode on, into the setting's TOML file with it off, as the TOML
would write the value. It may be called from any region thread; the
value is in force when the call returns and the file is written on the
configuration writer thread, so no region thread waits on the disk.

Before exiting, the server waits for that thread, so the last change
made before /stop is not lost.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

diff --git a/net/minecraft/server/dedicated/DedicatedServer.java b/net/minecraft/server/dedicated/DedicatedServer.java
index a01b8a111709dfddaace9a4b94e829a2ac513978..4df5619d00b0831201f5ccff93a3331847cd714c 100644
--- a/net/minecraft/server/dedicated/DedicatedServer.java
+++ b/net/minecraft/server/dedicated/DedicatedServer.java
@@ -538,6 +538,7 @@ public class DedicatedServer extends MinecraftServer implements ServerInterface
             }
         }
 
+        io.github.adrielorihuela.legacyfolia.config.ConfigHooks.stop(); // LegacyFolia - the last configuration change reaches the disk
         this.hasFullyShutdown = true; // Paper - Improved watchdog support
         System.exit(this.abnormalExit ? 70 : 0); // CraftBukkit // Paper - Improved watchdog support
     }
diff --git a/net/minecraft/server/dedicated/Settings.java b/net/minecraft/server/dedicated/Settings.java
index 178f750c114afe26c98ff3434e6837f0b5f40f65..439e3298ddeea78d15910e3e0c271b0ac987340f 100644
--- a/net/minecraft/server/dedicated/Settings.java
+++ b/net/minecraft/server/dedicated/Settings.java
@@ -274,6 +274,7 @@ public abstract class Settings<T extends Settings<T>> {
         public T update(final RegistryAccess registryAccess, final V value) {
             Properties properties = Settings.this.cloneProperties();
             properties.put(this.key, this.serializer.apply(value));
+            io.github.adrielorihuela.legacyfolia.config.ConfigHooks.vanillaChanged(this.key, this.serializer.apply(value)); // LegacyFolia - saved where the setting lives: server.properties with the mode on, its TOML file with it off
             return Settings.this.reload(registryAccess, properties, Settings.this.options); // CraftBukkit
         }
     }
